# Seeds for failure cases proptest has generated in the past. It is
# automatically read and these particular cases re-run before any
# novel cases are generated.
#
# It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
# everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases.
#
# HAND-EDITED (P23.3). proptest appends a `# shrinks to ...` comment carrying the
# whole shrunk input, and for this file that is a full `Mesh` Debug dump — 31 kB
# of arena across six seeds, for no reading benefit. The seeds are the
# load-bearing part; the dumps are replaced here by what each one actually found.
# Both defects also have named deterministic tests
# (`weld_relinks_every_vertex_the_patch_touched` in `ops`,
# `the_ear_chooser_avoids_a_diagonal_that_already_exists` in `export`): a seed
# says "this input broke it once", a named test says what the bug was.
#
# 1–5: a `WeldVerts`/`CollapseEdge` whose incident face lost its surface was not
#      rebuilt, so its vertices never reached `finish_patch` and boundary
#      half-edges elsewhere kept pointing at freed slots (`DeadLink`).
# 6:   the writer emitted an n-gon ear diagonal duplicating an edge the mesh
#      already had, so `from_mesh_asset` refused the writer's own output as
#      non-manifold.
# 7:   (audit round) UV handedness entered the corner-split key computed PER FACE
#      and from f64 UVs. Both were wrong: an n-gon whose UV loop sums to zero has
#      triangles that do not, and a sign taken in f64 disagrees with the f32 one
#      the reread recomputes — so `export_is_a_fixed_point` wrote 16 vertices and
#      re-wrote 18. Per triangle, from f32. See `uv_orientation`.
